indicator-keyboard_0.0.0+19.10.20240924-0ubuntu1+unity4_amd64.changes:
----------------------------------------------------------------------

Format: 1.8
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 10:16:00 +0000
Source: indicator-keyboard
Binary: indicator-keyboard
Built-For-Profiles: derivative.ubuntu noudeb
Architecture: amd64
Version: 0.0.0+19.10.20240924-0ubuntu1+unity4
Distribution: resolute
Urgency: medium
Maintainer: Ubuntu Developers <ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com>
Changed-By: Ubuntu Unity Life Support <mihail.rozshko@gmail.com>
Description:
 indicator-keyboard - Keyboard indicator
Changes:
 indicator-keyboard (0.0.0+19.10.20240924-0ubuntu1+unity4) resolute; urgency=medium
 .
   * lib/main.vala: do not rewrite the greeter's input sources while
     AccountsService has no data. When accounts-daemon restarts, the listed
     users are loaded with an empty cache for a fraction of a second, and
     migrate_input_sources() wrote sources=[] and current=list.size - 1
     (4294967295) over the greeter's layouts; a stored 4294967295 came back
     after a reboot as the last layout. The pass is now skipped while no
     counted user has data and redone on ActUserManager::user-changed. Users
     are listed afresh on every pass, and a manager notify::is-loaded handler
     is connected when the manager was already loaded at start too (an
     instance started inside the reload window never migrated again). Write
     sources before current, and only values that changed.
   * lib/input-sources.vala: greeter_sources_known() and greeter_current()
     (0 with no sources, the wanted index if in range, else the last).
   * tests: add greeter-sources-known and greeter-current.
